; SP15 3a calibration wave: the PACING CHECK fixture. 006.VID is the
; test-card source (tools\demo-files\1920x1080-25p.mp4) encoded at the
; SAME 16:9 320x192 letterbox shape as 003 - so it walks the same
; gapped decode path - but at test-card content density, so it paces
; with a large PACE margin. The card carries a rolling frame/timestamp
; banner, a big seconds digit AND a 1 Hz beep authored into the source
; audio, which makes it a two-dimensional instrument: beep-vs-stopwatch
; measures RATE, beep-vs-counter measures A/V SYNC. Exactly 5.000 s /
; 125 frames, so VPACL's loop rewind keeps the 1 Hz beep cadence
; continuous across passes - loop it N times for an N x 5 s stopwatch
; leg. (Verbs 92-95 were never assigned - the retired VSTG ladder used
; 88-91 and 96-100.)
VPACE   92      verb
VPACL   93      verb
; SP15 3b: RING STREAMING legs - long-clip fixtures BIGGER than the
; pool ring, staged by tests\build-tests.ps1 -VidLong (full-duration
; 10s research-clip encodes, 6.4-11MB, cached like the leg set):
;   VSTR0 - 007.VID classic 256x192 (Sintel 10s, ~6.4MB, 250 frames)
;   VSTR1 - 008.VID full 320x256 LOOPED (BBB 10s, ~11MB, 252 frames -
;           the long-clip seam-free-loop leg; any key exits)
;   VSTR2 - 009.VID 16:9 320x192 letterbox (Jellyfish 10s, ~7.3MB -
;           the GAPPED streaming path)
;   DPACE/DPACL - 011.VID classic-wide 256x133 --direct (the test
;           card, 5.000 s / 125 frames) - the DIRECT PACING CARD
;   VSTRU - 099.VID (a copy of 007): plain streamed regression leg -
;           the DEBUG throttle that once drove a deliberate-underrun
;           drill here is RETIRED (see the 3c NOTE below; git holds
;           the lever).
; 94-95 were never assigned; 96-97 reuse retired VSTG ladder numbers.
VSTR0   94      verb
VSTR1   95      verb
VSTR2   96      verb
VSTRU   97      verb

; SP15 3c DIRECT-SERVE legs (header hint, flags bit1): 010.VID =
; 256x133 all-literal raw-equivalent encode (Sintel full 10s, --direct),
; served straight from the SD wire to the surface - no ring, no RAM
; pass. VDIR plays once, VDIRL loops (the loop exercises the direct
; producer rewind + header-block consume). 98/99 reuse retired VSTG
; ladder numbers. NOTE (3c): the 099 deliberate-underrun THROTTLE lever
; behind VSTRU is RETIRED - VSTRU now plays 099.VID (the 007 copy) as an
; ordinary streamed regression leg; the drill's verdict is on record in
; Cards #3/#4 and git holds the lever.
; SP15 Card #5 TIGHTEN RULING (2026-07-26, owner-decided): the
; direct-serve gate is UNCONDITIONAL (no accept-slow override). The
; originally-shipped classic-wide 256x144@25 stereo scored 1.075 (~6%
; slow) and is refused outright by its own gate now; 010/VDIR/VDIRL are
; re-encoded at 256x133@25 stereo (util 0.99, TRUE at-rate).
VDIR    98      verb
VDIRL   99      verb
; SP15 Card #5: the DIRECT PACING CARD. 011.VID is the SAME test-card
; source and the SAME 5.000 s / 125 frames as 006.VID, encoded --direct
; at 010's 256x133 shape - so DPACL is to the direct path exactly what
; VPACL is to the delta paths: stopwatch on a beep, count N beeps, and
; the beep-vs-stopwatch split measures the direct RATE while
; beep-vs-counter measures A/V sync. Direct playback now runs TRUE
; at-rate (util 0.99, not the refused 1.075), so 12 loop passes (60 s
; nominal) should land at 60.0 s - the beep count now verifies direct
; mode plays at rate, not ~6% slow. 88/89 reuse retired VSTG ladder
; numbers.
DPACE   88      verb
DPACL   89      verb
; VSTG1-4 / VS2E / VS6 / VS7 / VS2F / VS2G (the SP14a staged-entry
; ladder + its sub-ladders, verbs 88-91 and 96-100 - 96/97 since
; reused by VSTR2/VSTRU above) are RETIRED with
; the v1 player they instrumented (SP15 3a): every stage gate they
; drove was deleted in the video.asm rewrite, their crash class was
; root-caused and closed (the cross-page store + copper-init
; postmortems), and the v2 player has its own timeline instrument
; rows instead. git holds the verbs and the ladder machinery.
; Silicon keyboard-defect task: KTEST is the owner's hardware-sweep
; instrument for the keyboard matrix/decode fix (see PRO 9 below and
; overlay1.asm's ktest_poll / overlay0.asm's EXTERN vector 6). DEBUG
; build only - Release's EXTERN 0 6 is ext_stub (silent no-op, blank
; screen, no crash); this verb is not meant to ship.
KTEST 101     verb

; Card #6 SNAP=03/00 sitting follow-up (.superpowers/sdd/sp14a-task-4-
; report.md section 41): the seven-leg sitting could not exercise
; vid_snap_geom's mode-0 (3-bank) or hidden-L2 (0-bank) branches - the
; test template always runs 320x256 mode-1, so SNAP=05 on every row.
; DEBUG build only owner instruments, EXTERN vectors 8/9/10
; (overlay0.asm's l2mod_trampoline/l2hide_trampoline/l2show_trampoline
; -> overlay2.asm's l2mod_run/l2_disable/l2_enable), Release's stubs
; are silent no-ops:
;   L2MOD - draws the mode-0 (256x192) DEBUG test card over the front
;     surface (l2_testcard's own gradient + corner markers - reused
;     rather than new drawing code). A following VPLY1 should then
;     read SNAP=03 and auto-return the card intact.
;   LHIDE - clears NR $69's Layer 2 visible bit (l2_disable), exactly
;     the bit vid_snap_geom reads. A following VPLY1 should then read
;     SNAP=00 (hidden-L2, zero pool cost) and exit clean, text-only.
;   LSHOW - re-sets it (l2_enable), undoing LHIDE.
L2MOD 90      verb
LHIDE 91      verb
LSHOW 100     verb

; SP17 T5 Layer 2 SCROLL bring-up (run sheet .superpowers/sdd/
; sp14a-task-4-report.md section 41.4). Ten DEBUG-only owner verbs on
; ONE EXTERN vector (11 - overlay0.asm's l2scr_trampoline ->
; overlay2.asm's l2scr_run), the parameter selecting a config row.
; Every one of them: paints the existing DEBUG test card + its marker
; blocks, then pans the Layer 2 hardware offset one step per frame
; until ANY key is pressed; on exit the offsets return to 0, the
; mode's full clip window is re-asserted and Layer 2 is hidden again
; (unlike L2MOD, which leaves its card up - a mode-1 card covers all
; but the bottom 16 lines, so leaving it up would mean typing the
; next row's verb blind). Verb numbers 102-111 are
; free (NXBEN's retired 102-116 block). Release's EXTERN 0 11 is
; ext_stub - a silent no-op.
;   LSX0/LSX1 - X offset wrap, mode-0 (256 wide) / mode-1 (320 wide,
;     the 9-bit NR $16 + NR $71 offset)
;   LSY0/LSY1 - Y offset wrap, mode-0 (192 high) / mode-1 (256 high)
;   LSCX/LSCY - the same pans under an inset clip window (all four
;     sides), mode-1: does the window stay put in SCREEN space?
;   LSTA/LSTB - tear pair, mode-0, coarse 8px step: identical except
;     LSTA writes the offset inside vblank and LSTB writes it with the
;     raster mid-picture
;   LSTC - same mid-raster write in mode-1, where the 9-bit offset
;     needs TWO non-atomic register writes
;   LS256 - static hold at exactly 256 (NR $71 bit 0 = 1, NR $16 = 0):
;     the MSB proof and the pan-direction sign
LSX0  102     verb
LSX1  103     verb
LSY0  104     verb
LSY1  105     verb
LSCX  106     verb
LSCY  107     verb
LSTA  108     verb
LSTB  109     verb
LSTC  110     verb
LS256 111     verb

; SP17 PLAYER BENCH (the NXBEN revival - card .superpowers/sdd/
; sp14a-task-4-report.md section 42). NXBEN itself was retired at SP15
; 3a: the format froze on its evidence and its prototype kernels
; graduated into the production decoder. The revival measures the
; SHIPPING routines instead of prototypes, so the rows answer decode
; questions the player actually has. Four verbs on the last of the old
; 102-116 block; the three standalone modes share EXTERN vector 12
; (overlay0.asm's nxb_trampoline -> video.asm's nxb_entry) with the
; mode in flag 250, and the fourth rides the PLAYER because its rows
; need a live armed direct-serve session.
;   NXBO - mode 2, op dispatch envelope (8 rows)
;   NXBC - mode 3, COPY kernel size ladder (9 rows)
;   NXBK - mode 4, fill crossover + DMA DI window (5 rows)
;   NXBD - flag 248 + GFX 10 13: the direct-serve transport
;          breakdown against 010.VID (6 rows). NEEDS -VidLong staged.
;          Playback is REPLACED by the bench - nothing plays.
; Rows print at tilemap rows 8+ and become visible when the timeline
; report hides Layer 2 at teardown. Release's EXTERN 0 12 is ext_stub
; and flag 248 is inert, so all four are silent no-ops there.
NXBO  112     verb
NXBC  113     verb
NXBK  114     verb
NXBD  115     verb

; BUILD WAVE W5 GRAND STAGING: numbered play. The staged library for
; the build-then-judge sitting is dozens of NNN.VID files - far more
; than fixed verbs can cover. PICK nn arms clip nn (the parsed noun's
; word value is copied into user flag 140); GO plays the armed clip
; once via GFX @140 13 (first-operand indirection - the engine
; dereferences flag 140 at dispatch, engine.asm:443); LOOP plays it
; looping via GFX @140 14 (any key exits). PLAY is a synonym of GO.
; The number words below make the numerals themselves vocabulary
; nouns with word value = the numeral (the parser tokenizes digits
; like letters - word_next, overlay1.asm - so "pick 23" parses as
; verb PICK + noun "23" = 23). Values 2-11/14/20 alias existing
; movement/INVEN/ALL nouns - harmless synonymy, only the VALUE is
; used. Range 1-64 + 99 covers the W5 manifest
; (.superpowers/sdd/sp17-corpus/w5-manifest.md holds the number map).
; Verb numbers 116-118: 116 is the last of the retired NXBEN block,
; 117-118 were never assigned.
PICK  116     verb
GO    117     verb
PLAY  117     verb
LOOP  118     verb
