; SP9 owner verbs: XMES is the eye verb for EXTERN vector 3
; (XMESSAGE) - also proves the template 0.XMB emission/staging wired
; in Task 3. AYBAD is the ear verb for the SFB bounds guard (Task 4):
; GAME.SFB has 6 effects and no 200.WAV exists, so effect 200 must be
; pure silence, never garbage tones.
> XMES    _     XMESSAGE "External message via 0.XMB - tokens, wrap and More paging all native."
                DONE

> AYBAD   _     SFX 200 1
                DONE

; SP10 owner verb: TUNE2 is the ear leg for the AYS streamed song - the
; too-big-for-AKY 002.AYS (via -Aud staging). SFX 2 7 loops the stream;
; STOPM (SFX 0 8) stops it (sub 8 now stops both music kinds).
> TUNE2   _     SFX 2 7
                DONE

; SP10 Task 5 owner verb, reworked SP11 (twice): MTEST is the
; eye/hardware leg for the Kempston mouse condact. MOUSE 0 1 uploads
; the arrow pattern (first call only, gated internally by mouseReady),
; arms NR $15 and shows/positions hardware sprite 0 - once, here, on
; entry. PROCESS 8 then drains the ENTER keypress that just SUBMITTED
; this "mtest" command line: that key is very often still physically
; down (or not yet reported released) the instant we get here, and
; without draining it, PRO 7's own exit check would read it as a fresh
; keypress and the loop would end after a single pass - the exact
; hardware symptom reported after the first fix landed ("pointer
; appears then disappears after each mtest"). Only once PRO 8 confirms
; no key is down does PROCESS 7 start the real loop: poll (MOUSE 120 3)
; into scratch flags 120-123 (buttons, X/8, Y/8, X/6), reprint them in
; place on the same screen spot, repeat - so the owner watches the
; values track live mouse movement instead of seeing one static
; snapshot. Flag 120 (buttons) is jdaad-parity, NOT the raw Kempston
; byte: idle 0, left click 1, right click 2, middle click 4, chords
; additive (e.g. left+right = 3) - h_mouse's .read transforms the raw
; active-LOW/Kempston-order port byte (idle would otherwise read 7,
; right/left swapped versus jdaad, plus nonzero wheel bits) to this
; convention at the flag-write point (src/overlay0.asm; jdaad.js
; _MOUSE/GetMouse is the parity authority). Any keypress made DURING
; that loop (INKEY, in PRO 7) ends
; it; the pointer is hidden (MOUSE 0 2) before the verb returns DONE.
; Under headless CSpect (no -mouse capture, or CSpect closed) the
; sprite still shows/positions and the flags still print - just
; static/zero without a live pointer - and a keypress still exits
; normally.
> MTEST   _     MOUSE 0 1
                PROCESS 8
                PROCESS 7
                DONE

; Silicon keyboard-defect task owner verb: KTEST is the hardware-sweep
; eye leg for the keyboard matrix decode fix (src/input.asm resident
; state, src/overlay1.asm kb_raw/kb_char, the CAPS+2 caps-lock toggle).
; No submission-key drain is needed here (unlike MTEST): KTEST's exit
; trigger is a SPECIFIC chord (TRUE VIDEO, CAPS+3), not "any key", so
; the stale ENTER that just submitted the "ktest" command line cannot
; false-trigger it. PROCESS 9 (see its own table, after PRO 8 below)
; runs the poll/draw/exit-check loop; CLS restores a normal text
; screen once it returns.
> KTEST   _     PROCESS 9
                CLS
                DONE

