; SP15 3a owner verbs: the NXV v2 player eye/ear legs. VPLY* exercises
; the GFX n 13 (play-once) real dispatch path (h_gfx sub 13,
; overlay2.asm -> vid_play, video.asm); VLOP* exercises GFX n 14
; (loop - seam-free by construction on the resident path, any key ends
; it). SPLY4 proves the SFX n 9 alias surface (h_sfx, overlay1.asm)
; reaches the SAME player. Fixture map (v2 shape matrix, -Vid):
;   VPLY0/VLOP0 - 001.VID full         320x256 mode-1 flat
;   VPLY1/VLOP1 - 002.VID classic      256x192 mode-0 flat
;   VPLY2/VLOP2 - 003.VID 16:9         320x192 mode-1 letterbox
;   VPLY3/VLOP3 - 004.VID scope        320x144 mode-1 letterbox
;   VPLY4/VLOP4 - 005.VID classic-wide 256x144 mode-0 letterbox
;   VPACE/VPACL - 006.VID 16:9         320x192 mode-1 letterbox
;                 (PACING CHECK: test card, 5.000 s / 125 frames /
;                  862,208 B; rolling counter + 1 Hz beep. VPACL loops
;                  it seamlessly - the beep cadence stays continuous
;                  across passes, so N loops = an N x 5 s stopwatch
;                  leg. Same gapped path as VPLY2 at a fraction of the
;                  decode cost, so PACE must be large and positive.)
; STAGE 3a: fixtures must fit the resident ring (see the vocabulary
; note; oversize = clean VID SIZE? exit, DEBUG). A DEBUG build with no
; staging fails silent (missing-file DEBUG marker only); Release is
; always silent. All video verbs finish with PROCESS 10 (post-video
; location art redraw) - the documented author convention: the player
; leaves the L2 surface to the game, the game redraws.
