; SP17 player bench (see the vocabulary block). The three standalone
; modes set flag 250 then share EXTERN 0 12; the mode cell self-clears
; in the handler, so a stray EXTERN can never re-run a row set. NXBD
; sets flag 248 and then plays 010.VID: the player opens the file
; exactly as it ships, and the bench hook diverts to the transport
; rows the instant the session is armed and BEFORE the CTC starts, so
; the rows are taken on a quiet machine. No PROCESS 10 on the three
; standalone verbs - they never touch the display, so there is
; nothing for the game to redraw.
> NXBO    _     LET     250 2
                EXTERN  0 12
                DONE

> NXBC    _     LET     250 3
                EXTERN  0 12
                DONE

> NXBK    _     LET     250 4
                EXTERN  0 12
                DONE

> NXBD    _     LET     248 1
                GFX     10 13
                PROCESS 10
                DONE

; BUILD WAVE W5 numbered play (see the vocabulary block note). PICK nn
; copies the parsed noun's word value (the numeral) into user flag 140
; - flag 140 is untouched by everything else in this template (120-123
; MTEST, 130 KTEST, 248/250 bench, 255 init loop) and survives across
; commands (PRO 6's flag-clearing loop only runs at game start). The
; NOTEQ guard rejects a missing/unknown number word (fNoun stays 255,
; NULLWORD) with a usage hint instead of arming clip 255. GO/PLAY and
; LOOP dereference the flag at dispatch (GFX @140 13/14 - condact 87
; with the indirection bit, so the DDB byte is $D7), guarded by
; NOTZERO so an un-armed GO prints the hint rather than hunting for
; 000.VID. Same PROCESS 10 post-video redraw convention as every
; other video verb.
> PICK    _     NOTEQ   fNoun 255
                COPYFF  fNoun 140
                MES "Clip "
                PRINT 140
                MES " armed - GO plays once, LOOP loops.#n"
                DONE

> PICK    _     MES "PICK needs a clip number, e.g. PICK 23 (see the W5 manifest).#n"
                DONE

> GO      _     NOTZERO 140
                GFX     @140 13
                PROCESS 10
                DONE

> GO      _     MES "No clip armed - PICK nn first.#n"
                DONE

> LOOP    _     NOTZERO 140
                GFX     @140 14
                PROCESS 10
                DONE

> LOOP    _     MES "No clip armed - PICK nn first.#n"
                DONE

